# Deploys run from the repo ROOT (the Vercel project's Root Directory is
# `storefront`), and Vercel only reads the top-level ignore file — nested
# .gitignore rules like storefront/.gitignore do NOT filter the upload. Without
# this file the local build caches get uploaded, which is ~670MB and trips the
# 100MB per-file limit on `.next/cache/webpack/*.pack`.

# Build output + caches (regenerated on Vercel)
**/.next
**/.next-verify
**/node_modules
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Coverage artifacts
**/*.profraw

# Legacy WordPress work — superseded by the Next.js storefront, never built
ecl-conversion/
hello-elementor-child/
migration/
